The '''Nemi language''' is a [[Kanak languages|Kanak language]] of the [[Austronesian languages|Austronesian language family]] spoken by 320 people in the north of [[New Caledonia]], in the commune of [[Hienghène]]. Dialects include Ouanga, Ouélis, and Kavatch.<ref>[[Isabelle Bril]], [[Françoise Ozanne-Rivierre]], ''Complex Predicates in Oceanic Languages: Studies in the Dynamics of Binding and Boundness'' (2012), p. 389.</ref>

